<p>Dallas hail damage claims are among the most common property insurance claims in North Texas, and the weather record shows why. The NOAA Storm Events Database lists 841 hail reports in Dallas County since 1955. Of those, 250 were golf-ball size (1.75 inches) or larger and 46 were baseball size (2.75 inches) or larger. Reports pile up from March through June, peak in April and May, and show a smaller second bump in October.</p>
<p>Hail damage is often harder to spot than people expect. Bruised shingles, fractured mats, and dented flashing usually cannot be seen from the driveway. The full scope may only show up during a close, slope-by-slope roof inspection. This page explains what a hail claim usually involves, where disputes tend to start, and how a public adjuster in Dallas may help. For the numbers behind hail season, read <a href="/dallas-hail-season-storm-data/">Dallas hail season storm data</a>.</p>

