<h2>Common Insurer Positions on Hail Claims</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>&ldquo;Wear and tear, not hail.&rdquo;</strong> The insurer attributes granule loss or cracking to age, blistering, or manufacturing issues. Long North Texas summers age shingles, which gives this argument traction.</li>
<li><strong>&ldquo;Prior storm.&rdquo;</strong> The carrier says the damage came from an earlier storm, one before the policy period, or one that was not reported promptly.</li>
<li><strong>&ldquo;Cosmetic only.&rdquo;</strong> Dents on metal roofing or soft metals are labeled cosmetic under an exclusion endorsement.</li>
<li><strong>Repair instead of replace.</strong> The estimate allows spot repairs even when brittle or discontinued shingles cannot be repaired or matched.</li>
<li><strong>Missing line items.</strong> Drip edge, starter course, ridge cap, flashing, permits, and code-required items are left off. Our <a href="/services/insurance-estimate-review/">insurance estimate review</a> looks for these gaps.</li>
</ul>
<p>If the claim was denied outright, see our <a href="/services/denied-insurance-claims/">denied insurance claims</a> page for next steps.</p>

<h2>Settlement Factors to Understand</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Wind/hail deductibles.</strong> Often a percentage of the dwelling limit, not a flat amount. Check your declarations page before you compare estimates.</li>
<li><strong>ACV vs. replacement cost.</strong> Under replacement cost coverage, insurers typically pay actual cash value first and release recoverable depreciation after repairs are finished, often within a deadline stated in the policy. Some Texas roof coverage is ACV-only or follows a roof payment schedule. See <a href="/replacement-cost-vs-actual-cash-value-texas/">replacement cost vs. actual cash value in Texas</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Code upgrades.</strong> Re-roofing in the city generally requires a permit through the City of Dallas Planning &amp; Development Department, and suburbs such as Garland, Richardson, and Irving have their own permit offices. Code-required work is paid only if your policy includes ordinance or law coverage, up to its limit. See <a href="/local-building-codes/">local building codes</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p>Personal property, other structures, and additional living expenses each have their own limits, so look at every coverage section, not only the dwelling limit.</p>

<h2>How Dallas Public Adjuster Can Help</h2>
<p>Dallas Public Adjuster is a public adjusting service of Rise Public Adjusting LLC, licensed by the Texas Department of Insurance (license #[[license]]). A licensed public adjuster represents the policyholder, not the insurance company. On a hail claim, that can include inspecting the roof and exterior, reviewing the policy, gathering weather data, preparing a detailed estimate, and communicating with the insurer&rsquo;s adjuster. If the claim was already paid low, we can review it for an <a href="/services/insurance-claim-supplements/">insurance claim supplement</a> or discuss whether <a href="/services/insurance-appraisal/">appraisal</a> fits a disagreement over the amount of loss. We cannot guarantee a result. Fees are disclosed in a written contract before any work begins; Texas law caps public adjuster compensation at 10% of the insurance settlement.</p>

<h2>Your Responsibilities After a Hailstorm</h2>
<ul>
<li>Give prompt notice to your insurer.</li>
<li>Protect the property from further damage (tarp openings, board broken windows) and keep every receipt.</li>
<li>Photograph damage before repairs and save samples of damaged materials when practical.</li>
<li>Submit a proof of loss if requested, within the time your policy requires.</li>
<li>Cooperate with inspections and reasonable requests for documents.</li>
</ul>
<p>Be cautious with door-to-door roofers after a big storm, and read anything before you sign it. Many policies also set a contractual deadline to file suit. For legal questions about deadlines or a dispute with your insurer, consult a Texas attorney.</p>
